[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to HTTP Response Splitting. This vulnerability arises because the function directly inserts user-provided content into HTTP response headers without properly validating or sanitizing it. Since HTTP headers restrict certain characters like carriage return (\r) and line feed (\n), untrusted input containing these can lead to header injection, allowing attackers to manipulate responses or inject malicious content.

